  "description": "This Egyptian black-eyed pea salad with cumin-lime dressing is quick, make-ahead–friendly, and loaded with crisp vegetables, briny olives, and herbs.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 1/2 teaspoon red pepper flakes (optional)\n\nOptional substitutions: distilled white vinegar → red wine vinegar; yellow pepper → red bell pepper; coarsely chopped pitted Kalamata olives → green olives; finely chopped fresh cilantro → parsley\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Dressing can be made up to 4 days in advance and refrigerated in an airtight container.\nSalad can be prepared, omitting the herbs, up to 4 days in advance and refrigerated in an airtight container. Add herbs just before serving.\nLeftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days, though herbs may become slightly wilted.",
